            {
                "entry_id": "34c4653b-fdfb-383a-be57-83638ce50ad8",
                "word": "pharisaïsme",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "3c3ef3ac-6d23-47a8-9ac2-b1144220286f",
                        "entry_id": "34c4653b-fdfb-383a-be57-83638ce50ad8",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "pharisaïsmes"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "1a605f25-a26f-4749-9f95-1af1c812e284",
                        "entry_id": "34c4653b-fdfb-383a-be57-83638ce50ad8",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "pharisianisme"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a73e050d-52de-390e-810e-c208d4a0fd68",
                        "entry_id": "34c4653b-fdfb-383a-be57-83638ce50ad8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Doctrine, attitude des pharisiens, qui consiste à surveiller uniquement le respect de la loi (les actes), sans tenir compte de son esprit (l'intention, le but)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "04af7681-f2f8-4c45-9a36-05fb95d7abf0",
                                "sense_id": "a73e050d-52de-390e-810e-c208d4a0fd68",
                                "text": "Demandons donc à Dieu de nous purifier du pharisaïsme des oeuvres, de la comptabilité de nos mérites, du souci de notre perfection et de notre salut afin que nous n'ayons qu'une préoccupation : celle de ne jamais blesser Son Amour et de laisser Sa Vie s'exprimer dans la nôtre."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "550f609f-933d-3a43-8f66-84c575d6b84b",
                        "entry_id": "34c4653b-fdfb-383a-be57-83638ce50ad8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Piété ostentatoire ; hypocrisie en religion."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7d319682-68f8-4946-880f-de4fdff1e828",
                                "sense_id": "550f609f-933d-3a43-8f66-84c575d6b84b",
                                "text": "Si les moralités dont nous avons parlé n’ont pas été un frein pour le débordement des puissants, si elles ont aggravé seulement le pharisaïsme de leurs mœurs en nécessitant qu’un voile d’hypocrisie fût jeté sur le mystère de leurs alcôves, combien n’ont-elles point causé de désespoirs, de douleurs inutiles, de remords absurdes, de perversions, de suicides et de crimes chez les faibles et les sincères […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e60e4843-9e4f-4862-9065-47ecd74462be",
                                "sense_id": "550f609f-933d-3a43-8f66-84c575d6b84b",
                                "text": "Ah ! le temps joyeux de la stupidité, du pharisaïsme à rebours où les petits messieurs pressés se hissaient paisiblement sur la crête de la notoriété. Tous des faiseurs, tous des faisans."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "905c7a5b-d90b-4958-b34f-5e39e6e09e83",
                                "sense_id": "550f609f-933d-3a43-8f66-84c575d6b84b",
                                "text": "Elle blâmait encore le pharisaïsme de son milieu, mais sans condamner toute l’humanité."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "29ce1272-6415-3cd8-8f62-dfa55f74f6ad",
                        "entry_id": "34c4653b-fdfb-383a-be57-83638ce50ad8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Vertu ostentatoire ; comportement utilisé pour se décrire publiquement comme une personne ou une organisation vertueuse."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1532c91d-363b-4ed0-a7ac-63c9f12f0437",
                                "sense_id": "29ce1272-6415-3cd8-8f62-dfa55f74f6ad",
                                "text": "Certains voient dans le politiquement correct un pharisaïsme moderne."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3153f436-8e35-45b6-a41d-6cc8accda217",
                        "source_entry_id": "34c4653b-fdfb-383a-be57-83638ce50ad8",
                        "target_lang_word": "pharisaism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pharisaism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d0781a89-bfaf-35df-be0e-2b7feab79ebb",
                                        "entry_id": "563ea531-b202-3a5d-b221-0cc36f4bc8d1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The doctrines and practices, or the character and spirit, of the Pharisees."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b86aae5c-595c-40cf-8b77-5a986e60c05e",
                                                "sense_id": "d0781a89-bfaf-35df-be0e-2b7feab79ebb",
                                                "text": "Since Paul lived and worked in the greater Syrian area as a Pharisee, it is somewhat probable that Pharisaism had some influence there and that some Pharisees lived outside Jerusalem and Judea. […] Paul never says where he made contact with Pharisaism, in Tarsus, Syria, or Jerusalem. […] The evidence concerning Pharisaism is so slim that we do not know how Paul came to know about Pharisaism, why he was attracted to it, and what being a Pharisee entailed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "761423bb-f7b9-4b0b-abc1-065125154d92",
                                                "sense_id": "d0781a89-bfaf-35df-be0e-2b7feab79ebb",
                                                "text": "Serious and substantial doubts about Paul's former life as a Pharisee, or even any contact with pharisaism on his part, have been raised."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8cd7aae3-80c8-3bcc-8a8e-d045aa074e8f",
                                        "entry_id": "563ea531-b202-3a5d-b221-0cc36f4bc8d1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Rigid observance of external forms of religion without genuine piety; hypocrisy in religion; a censorious, self-righteous spirit in matters of morals or manners."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd6d0c4b-a0b8-493f-b24d-1c45c1a3d802",
                                                "sense_id": "8cd7aae3-80c8-3bcc-8a8e-d045aa074e8f",
                                                "text": "[T]he Phariſee faſted twice every weeke, and that never cenſured in him as a peice of Phariſaiſme, or hypocriſie, or fault of any kind; but as commendable, if he had not boaſted of it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7c7a4667-cbec-4e56-9616-202cbf7a4df9",
                                                "sense_id": "8cd7aae3-80c8-3bcc-8a8e-d045aa074e8f",
                                                "text": "But denunciations do not go far, and the only living and effective protest would be a society itself delivered from all pharisaisms and idolatries."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "985869fe-b84b-4dc9-ac1f-7d3827ed2ee8",
                                                "sense_id": "8cd7aae3-80c8-3bcc-8a8e-d045aa074e8f",
                                                "text": "The codes of some modern pharisaism comprise mostly some virtues and moral rules selected from the codes of the Christian pharisaisms which they oppose […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4b8fbfef-8a0d-4058-bf9f-1657b0cb4715",
                        "source_entry_id": "34c4653b-fdfb-383a-be57-83638ce50ad8",
                        "target_lang_word": "virtue signalling",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "virtue signalling",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e9540671-680c-39eb-bf75-baeb50240337",
                                        "entry_id": "467ee24f-e860-389d-a8f2-0ad3c5bb9a30",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The practice of expressing a particular opinion or performing a particular action in an attempt to make oneself look virtuous: commonly defensively in response to, or anticipation of, criticism; or aggressively, in assuming a moral posture in attacking an opponent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e7e9794c-cbd8-48ff-a4c6-b28982cc0195",
                                                "sense_id": "e9540671-680c-39eb-bf75-baeb50240337",
                                                "text": "People of poor personal character may mistake all virtue for virtue signalling because they cannot even imagine anyone truly having the relevant virtues but they are quite familiar with the concept of pretending to have traits for malevolent reasons."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b20d7756-879a-4c0a-bb98-1b981df48de3",
                                                "sense_id": "e9540671-680c-39eb-bf75-baeb50240337",
                                                "text": "Corporate Social Responsibility as Competitive Virtue Signalling: Ethical Implications"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c249f843-2437-4c48-b990-7760d3fd8883",
                                                "sense_id": "e9540671-680c-39eb-bf75-baeb50240337",
                                                "text": "The poster goes on to assert: ‘We are part of a growing consciousness that is bigger than food — one that champions what’s good.’ This a particularly blatant example of the increasingly common phenomenon of what might be called ‘virtue signalling’ — indicating that you are kind, decent and virtuous."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "55fad2ca-b6e2-45a3-8e84-d18b9afaeaec",
                                                "sense_id": "e9540671-680c-39eb-bf75-baeb50240337",
                                                "text": "Conservative assembly member Andrew Boff said the ban was “reckless” at a time when TfL was facing a £1 billion deficit. “This is yet another example of the Mayor indulging in pointless virtue signalling and grandstanding,” he said."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "596fc1fc-5fdd-4b6c-a533-7119796e75f3",
                                                "sense_id": "e9540671-680c-39eb-bf75-baeb50240337",
                                                "text": "Virtue-signalling, for those who have never felt drawn to the term, is the apparently modern crime of trying to be seen doing the right thing. The implication is that the virtue-signaller does not really believe what they are saying but simply wishes to be admired as a good person."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "728499d5-bd02-41d6-b536-94bac75447b3",
                                                "sense_id": "e9540671-680c-39eb-bf75-baeb50240337",
                                                "text": "Sometimes, she’s sceptical: the virtue-signalling can be a little forced, a little on point. She names no names, obviously, but describes, tantalisingly, \"a couple of people who are like real activists, really at the forefront of progress, and I’m like, 'You are a deplorable fraud! And all you really care about is people looking at you.'\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c45a234-994e-4fee-a162-5c87dcd20457",
                                                "sense_id": "e9540671-680c-39eb-bf75-baeb50240337",
                                                "text": "The virtue-signaling invites cynicism over whether it is actually just a new means of advertising to Gen Z and millennials, two consumer groups deeply invested in issues of gender, sexuality and race."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "357aef91-6be5-4211-b78b-94d28373636c",
                                                "sense_id": "e9540671-680c-39eb-bf75-baeb50240337",
                                                "text": "The governor went to have a dig at Trump. “Government is not entertainment,” he said. “It’s not about building a brand or virtue signaling.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "virtue signalling",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "108a7fba-43a2-3675-8a8d-15bc32dc7511",
                                        "entry_id": "85f0e31a-b271-331b-a1cb-bb253d28e607",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "present participle and gerund of virtue signal"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "form-of",
                                            "gerund",
                                            "participle",
                                            "present"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
